    {
      "text": "To begin configuring Digital Experience (ZDX), you must first deploy the minimum required or later version of Zscaler Client Connector based on your OS."
    },
    {
      "text": "To configure Zscaler Client Connector for your organization, see What Is Zscaler Client Connector? and Step-by-Step Configuration Guide for Zscaler Client Connector."
    },
    {
      "text": "Zscaler supports the latest software version and the two previous versions for Zscaler Client Connector due to the commitment of continuous improvement for Zscaler products. To learn more, see Supported Versions, and Viewing and Configuring ZDX Module Upgrades."
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional prerequisites might also be required to access or use certain features. These can include:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Ranges & Limitations: To ensure the feature is supported by your subscription level.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "ZDX Role: To ensure you have the proper permissions for feature access.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "To determine if a feature requires additional prerequisites, see the feature's respective help articles."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Minimum OS Version Compatibility",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Each OS with a base ZDX Module version requires a compatible Zscaler Client Connector version."
    },
    {
      "table": [
        [
          "OS",
          "Zscaler Client Connector Version",
          "Base ZDX Module Version"
        ],
        [
          "Windows",
          "2.2.1",
          "1.0.0"
        ],
        [
          "macOS",
          "2.2.1",
          "1.0.0"
        ],
        [
          "Android",
          "1.12",
          "1.0.0"
        ],
        [
          "Android on ChromeOS",
          "1.12",
          "1.0.0"
        ],
        [
          "iOS",
          "3.8",
          "3.6"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If you have the base ZDX Module version with the respective Zscaler Client Connector version per OS, then you have access to the following in the Zscaler Admin Console:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Dashboard",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Analytics",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Applications",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Users",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Configuration",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Administration",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Alerts",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Search",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Activation",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Profile",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "Specific features (e.g., Software Inventory) require a later version compatibility or they are not available to the OS (e.g., Software and Device Inventory is unavailable for Android)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Supported Versions & Feature Compatibility",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Some ZDX features require a Zscaler Client Connector version for certain OS as indicated. The feature version compatibility is applicable to later versions (e.g., Software and Device Inventory requires a Zscaler Client Connector version 3.7.1.56 or later for Windows). If your organization does not meet the required feature version compatibility, upgrade your Zscaler Client Connector or ZDX Module as required."
    },
